# Recorded so the fixture's drift is detectable rather than silent.
# A SNAPSHOT of shani-settings/etc/audit/rules.d/10-shani-base.rules at
# shani-settings commit d21bd414f010325ebfcf1ea0717f20ec5de1748d. iso-install --console-put uses it to prove
# the rules load into a real kernel, which nspawn cannot: it shares a host
# kernel that refuses every audit netlink request from this environment.
#
# shani-settings is not bind-mounted into the harness container (see the
# loop in run_in_container.sh), so a copy is the only way --console-put can
# reach the file. If shani-settings changes it, re-copy and update this
# line - never test a stale snapshot and call it the current ruleset.
sha256  62b93477b486497e1396db300a087778a44518b7106544cd05420cef9fe5a266
commit  d21bd414f010325ebfcf1ea0717f20ec5de1748d
rules   64   (-a and -w lines: what the kernel load counts)
